# Agent-local and machine-local state. Nothing here is shared, and committing it
# would put per-machine settings and generated output into the lint scope and the
# plugin package. See specs/001-quality-gate-plugin/spec.md FR-018.

# Claude Code: consumer-side state, not this repository's authored content
.claude/logs/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/prompt.md

# Spec Kit: machine-local run state and per-checkout feature pointer
.specify/.speckit-run-state.json
.specify/.speckit-dirty-snapshot
.specify/feature.json

# Spec Kit extensions: machine-local working state only. Everything else the six
# extensions produce is committed on purpose -- see FR-027 and
# specs/001-quality-gate-plugin/research.md section 19. In particular
# .specify/extensions.yml, .specify/extensions/, .specify/assessments/ and
# .specify/bugs/ are project history, not state.
#
# The downloaded catalog, cached per machine. A 212 KB snapshot of
# raw.githubusercontent.com with a `cached_at` timestamp, refetched on demand and
# stale the moment upstream publishes. .registry is NOT here: that records which
# extensions are installed at which version, which is exactly what another
# checkout needs to reproduce this one.
.specify/extensions/.cache/

# token-budget writes <artifact>.full.md alongside each artifact it compacts, as
# a restore point for /speckit.token-budget.restore. A backup of one machine's
# pre-compaction copy is not a decision anyone needs to review.
*.full.md

# Agent memory
.remember/

# Dependency directories, fetched rather than authored
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/

# Tool caches
.ruff_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Self-test fixtures. Deliberately non-conforming, created and removed by
# scripts/selftest.sh. Also excluded by every check's own declaration --
# both are required, and neither alone is enough: this entry keeps a fixture
# from being committed, and the declarations keep the checks from examining
# one while it exists.
.lint-selftest-tmp/
